    "golden-5-tech-answer": {
      "text": "The short answer is that your loop allocates a new list on every iteration, which forces the garbage collector to run far more often than it should. Move the allocation outside the loop and reuse the buffer. In my tests that single change cut the run time from ninety seconds to eleven. If you need the intermediate results, preallocate the outer list with a known capacity instead of appending blindly. And measure before you optimise anything else: the profiler output you posted shows almost all the remaining time is spent in string formatting, not in the numeric code you were worried about.",
